# What never needs to reach a docker build context.
#
# Added by CHRN-25, when asr/Dockerfile started building a Go binary and
# therefore had to be built from the repository root rather than from its own
# directory. Both images are built from this context now, and neither wants any
# of the below.
#
# Kept SHORT and obviously-irrelevant on purpose. A .dockerignore that excludes
# source is a .dockerignore that produces a build failure nobody can reproduce
# outside Docker, so nothing here is a file either binary compiles.

# Local build output, already in .gitignore.
/bin/
/chronicle
*.test
coverage.*

# History. Neither image reads it: the build identity comes in as VERSION and
# GIT_SHA build args, precisely so an image cannot claim a version from a tree
# it was not built from.
.git/
.github/

# Benchmark evidence. CSVs and the harness that produced them, which belong in
# the repository and not in an image layer.
/asr/bench/results/

# Local environment. Never in an image, and never in a context that could put
# one in an image by accident.
.env
.env.*
